# Sarcosine.
# While this params file is technically redundant, since we have GLY:N_METHYLATION, we need it for design, since Rosetta cannot currently design with variant types.
# Added 14 May 2024 by Vikram K. Mulligan, CCB, Flatiron Institute (vmulligan@flatironinstitute.org).
NAME SAR
IO_STRING SAR X
TYPE POLYMER
AA UNK
ATOM  N   Nbb  NXX  -0.49
ATOM  CA  CAbb CT2  -0.14
ATOM  C   CObb C    0.66
ATOM  O   OCbb O    -0.51
ATOM  CA1 CH2  CT2  -0.14
ATOM 1HA1 Hapo HA   0.13
ATOM 2HA1 Hapo HA   0.13
ATOM 3HA1 Hapo HA   0.13
ATOM 1HA2 Hapo HA   0.13
ATOM 2HA2 Hapo HA   0.13
BOND  N    CA 
BOND  CA1 1HA1
BOND  CA1 2HA1
BOND  CA1 3HA1
BOND  CA1  N  
BOND  CA  1HA2
BOND  CA  2HA2
BOND  CA   C  
BOND  O    C  
LOWER_CONNECT N
UPPER_CONNECT C
CHI 1  CA   N    CA1  1HA1 
PROTON_CHI 1 SAMPLES 3 -150 150 180 EXTRA 1 20
NBR_ATOM  CA1 
NBR_RADIUS 4.5 
FIRST_SIDECHAIN_ATOM  CA1
PROPERTIES PEPTOID ACHIRAL_BACKBONE ACHIRAL_SIDECHAIN ALIPHATIC
RAMA_PREPRO_FILENAME scoring/score_functions/rama/n_methyl/sarcosine_ramatable_MM.txt scoring/score_functions/rama/n_methyl/sarcosine_ramatable_prepro_MM.txt
RAMA_PREPRO_RESNAME GENERIC_NMETHYLGLYCINE_AA
